{
  "video_id": "qLGedP9hXNg",
  "title": "How I cut my Claude Code bill to zero",
  "description": "Graphify is a free open source tool with 106,510 GitHub stars that scans your codebase once and builds a knowledge graph of how everything connects. Claude Code then navigates that map instead of re-reading every file each session, which cuts the context spent on orientation dramatically. It uses deterministic parsing rather than embeddings, runs entirely on your own device under Apache 2.0, and installs a hook so it works automatically without you remembering to use it.\n\nGet the full setup here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fTaFzux4H-UqgUVt-S5mN5Nz7pRa2_l2Cy6GKnmrTFs/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #ClaudeCode #OpenSource",
  "publishedAt": "2026-08-18T08:13:58Z",
  "channel_name": "Sebastian Hardy | AI Marketing",
  "transcript": "Graphify is a free open source tool with 106,510 GitHub stars that scans your codebase once and builds a knowledge graph of how everything connects. Claude Code then navigates that map instead of re-reading every file each session, which cuts the context spent on orientation dramatically. It uses deterministic parsing rather than embeddings, runs entirely on your own device under Apache 2.0, and installs a hook so it works automatically without you remembering to use it.\n\nGet the full setup here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fTaFzux4H-UqgUVt-S5mN5Nz7pRa2_l2Cy6GKnmrTFs/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #ClaudeCode #OpenSource",
